      <div class="case-content">
        <section id="abstract">
          <h2>Abstract</h2>
          <p>
            Local agentic coding workflows increasingly span heterogeneous CLI agents—each backed by distinct model families, billing structures, and rolling subscription quotas (e.g., 5-hour and 7-day rate-limit windows). Running these tools independently forces developers to manually switch terminals, loses cross-session context, wastes substantial context tokens on raw file reads and verbose CLI output, and lacks deterministic safeguards against tool-call loops.
          </p>
          <p>
            We present <strong>Cockpit (<code>agent-orchestrator</code>)</strong>, a native Rust + GPUI desktop orchestrator and concurrent stdio Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that unifies Claude Code, Codex CLI, Antigravity, and OpenCode behind a single workspace, live quota telemetry layer, and deterministic token-efficiency harness. Across an offline ablation suite run directly on Cockpit's own Rust codebase, structural skeletons cut tokens by <strong>94.13%</strong> on average (up to <strong>97.07%</strong> on <code>app.rs</code> in 38.0 ms), CLI filtering cuts verbose logs by <strong>84.94%</strong> (<strong>96.83%</strong> on 123-test <code>cargo test</code> output), context compaction reduces an 18-turn session by <strong>88.34%</strong> (Capsule) and <strong>97.31%</strong> (5-line handoff), observation masking cuts stale tool output by <strong>69.51%</strong>, <code>LoopGuard</code> catches <strong>3/3</strong> loops with <strong>0 false positives</strong>, and deterministic routing achieves <strong>100.0%</strong> accuracy in <code>&lt; 20 µs</code>. All invariants pass <strong>139 Rust unit tests</strong> (16 core + 123 runtime).
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="intro-related">
          <h2>1. Introduction &amp; 2. Related Work</h2>
          <p>
            Operating heterogeneous CLIs concurrently exposes four systemic bottlenecks that model scaling alone does not solve: context bloat from raw reads and logs, search-and-replace edit fragility, silent tool-call loops, and fragmented 5h/7d quota visibility across providers. Cockpit addresses these bottlenecks at the local systems layer, building on empirical findings from:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Structural Localization:</strong> <em>AutoCodeRover</em> (<code>arXiv:2404.05427</code>), <em>Agentless</em> (<code>arXiv:2407.01489</code>), <em>RepoGraph</em> (<code>arXiv:2410.14684</code>), and <em>LocAgent</em> (<code>arXiv:2503.09089</code>) — operationalized in pure Rust (<code>fs_skeleton</code>, symbol-annotated <code>fs_search</code>, <code>blast_radius</code>) with sub-40 ms latency and zero external indexer daemon.</li>
            <li><strong>Diff Interfaces &amp; External Oracles:</strong> <em>Diff-XYZ</em> (<code>arXiv:2510.12487</code>), Huang et al. (<code>arXiv:2310.01798</code>), and <em>TDD-Bench Verified</em> (<code>arXiv:2412.02883</code>) — applied via hash-anchored reads (<code>hashline</code>), inline compiler verification (<code>fs_patch(..., verify: true)</code>), and pre-merge Git worktree quality gates.</li>
            <li><strong>Quota-Aware Routing &amp; Multi-Agent Scaling Limits:</strong> <em>RouteLLM</em> (<code>arXiv:2406.18665</code>), <em>MasRouter</em> (<code>arXiv:2502.11133</code>), <em>Puppeteer</em> (<code>arXiv:2505.19591</code>), <em>MAST</em> (<code>arXiv:2503.13657</code>), and <em>Towards a Science of Scaling Agent Systems</em> (<code>arXiv:2512.08296</code>) — motivating single-agent defaults, bounded delegation depth (<code>COCKPIT_DELEGATE_DEPTH=1</code>), and live quota-weighted routing.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="architecture">
          <h2>3. System Architecture</h2>
          <div class="arch-stack" role="img" aria-label="Three-layer Cockpit Rust workspace architecture: orchestrator-ui, orchestrator-runtime, and orchestrator-core">
            <div class="arch-layer">
              <div class="arch-layer-head">
                <strong>orchestrator-ui</strong>
                <span>GPUI CE 0.3.0 · Native Desktop UI</span>
              </div>
              <ul class="arch-layer-grid">
                <li>Multi-project chat &amp; adaptive left timeline (sparse / prop / dense)</li>
                <li>Unified &amp; Side-by-Side diff review + inline agent line comments</li>
                <li>Live 90s quota telemetry &amp; per-model visual hover cards</li>
                <li>Floating planning drawer (&gt;5 tasks) &amp; Worktree Diff / Gate / Merge UI</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="arch-flow" aria-hidden="true">↓ tokio channels &amp; atomic state</div>

            <div class="arch-layer arch-layer--runtime">
              <div class="arch-layer-head">
                <strong>orchestrator-runtime</strong>
                <span>Supervision, Routing, Concurrent MCP &amp; Safety</span>
              </div>
              <ul class="arch-layer-grid">
                <li><code>agent_runner.rs</code> · Headless CLI spawner (hidden Windows processes)</li>
                <li><code>mcp_server.rs</code> · Concurrent stdio MCP (<code>fs_*</code>, batch, delegate)</li>
                <li><code>code_intel.rs</code> · Pure-Rust <code>fs_skeleton</code>, repomap, <code>blast_radius</code></li>
                <li><code>cli_filter.rs</code> · Output compression, stacktrace &amp; log folding</li>
                <li><code>compact_context.rs</code> · KV-cache-safe capsules, 5-line handoffs, masking</li>
                <li><code>loop_guard.rs</code> · Sliding-window repeat/error/oscillation guard</li>
                <li><code>router.rs</code> · Quota-aware model/subagent routing + benchmarks</li>
                <li><code>worktree.rs</code> + <code>accounts.rs</code> · Git worktrees, quality gates, 5h/7d quotas</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="arch-flow" aria-hidden="true">↓ NDJSON streaming</div>

            <div class="arch-layer">
              <div class="arch-layer-head">
                <strong>orchestrator-core</strong>
                <span>Unified Event Schema &amp; NDJSON Parsers</span>
              </div>
              <ul class="arch-layer-grid">
                <li>Unified engines: Claude Code · Codex CLI · Antigravity (<code>agy</code>) · OpenCode v2.3</li>
                <li>Normalized events: <code>ThinkingDelta</code> · <code>ToolActivity</code> · <code>FileTouched</code> · <code>Usage</code></li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>
            Long-running MCP tools (<code>cockpit_delegate_agent</code>, <code>cockpit_benchmark_models</code>, <code>cockpit_self_rebuild</code>) run on dedicated worker threads synchronized over <code>Arc&lt;Mutex&lt;Stdout&gt;&gt;</code> so parallel delegations never stall fast <code>fs_*</code> calls. Exclusive per-file TTL leases guard concurrent writes, while <code>compact_context.rs</code> preserves a byte-identical <code>static_prefix</code> for KV-cache reuse.
          </p>
        </section>

