        <section id="validity">
          <h2>6. Threats to Validity &amp; 7. Conclusion</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Offline Token Proxy vs. Vendor Tokenizers:</strong> <code>ceil(chars / 4)</code> may differ by ±5–10% from provider-specific BPE tokenizers, while 69%–97% compression ratios remain structurally stable because byte volume drops equivalently.</li>
            <li><strong>Controlled E2E Solve-Rate Ablation:</strong> Deterministic ablations isolate compression, loop detection, and routing latency with zero variance; Section 5.3 reports observational telemetry rather than a randomized SWE-bench trial (planned future work).</li>
            <li><strong>Platform &amp; Source Scope:</strong> Cockpit targets Windows desktop workflows and resides in a private repository (<code>agent-orchestrator</code>). Future work covers paired E2E evaluations, automatic per-subagent worktree isolation, and cross-model diff verification.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

